[
 {
  "id": "n01a",
  "text": "Every record on Propchain is attested.",
  "file": "vo/n01a_1f52941810.mp3",
  "dur": 2.456,
  "in": 0,
  "out": 2.184,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.034,
    2.064
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n01b",
  "text": "But attestation proves provenance, not truth. A rent roll full of phantom tenants can be perfectly signed, and perfectly false.",
  "file": "vo/n01b_5650b746bf.mp3",
  "dur": 8.725,
  "in": 0.042,
  "out": 8.193,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.082,
    2.825
   ],
   [
    3.439,
    5.281
   ],
   [
    5.554,
    6.776
   ],
   [
    6.971,
    8.073
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n02",
  "text": "And consensus can't decide whether a tenant exists.",
  "file": "vo/n02_59ac015f6e.mp3",
  "dur": 3.892,
  "in": 0.051,
  "out": 3.854,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.091,
    3.097
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n03",
  "text": "Most fraud loss is misstated income, or diverted closing funds. Both have a truth the platform can see: cash.",
  "file": "vo/n03_47b4170497.mp3",
  "dur": 8.307,
  "in": 0,
  "out": 7.747,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.011,
    2.187
   ],
   [
    2.453,
    3.985
   ],
   [
    4.744,
    6.848
   ],
   [
    7.152,
    7.627
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n04",
  "text": "The aim is to make lies expensive, and detectable.",
  "file": "vo/n04_1eea8215f8.mp3",
  "dur": 3.187,
  "in": 0.061,
  "out": 2.856,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.101,
    2.736
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n05",
  "text": "The defence is six layers, each stopping what the one below cannot: identity, provenance, corroboration, bonds, professional signatures, and memory.",
  "file": "vo/n05_8f4961eb16.mp3",
  "dur": 10.762,
  "in": 0.046,
  "out": 10.217,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.086,
    1.526
   ],
   [
    1.809,
    3.911
   ],
   [
    4.461,
    5.158
   ],
   [
    5.362,
    5.904
   ],
   [
    6.074,
    6.902
   ],
   [
    7.145,
    7.629
   ],
   [
    8.019,
    9.227
   ],
   [
    9.483,
    10.097
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n06",
  "text": "What gets through all six is what insurance prices.",
  "file": "vo/n06_1cba018dd9.mp3",
  "dur": 3.579,
  "in": 0.049,
  "out": 3.066,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.089,
    2.946
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n07",
  "text": "Corroboration first. One asset's annual rent, from four sources.",
  "file": "vo/n07_1b5b8defcb.mp3",
  "dur": 4.624,
  "in": 0,
  "out": 4.187,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.025,
    1.204
   ],
   [
    1.542,
    4.067
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n08",
  "text": "The rent roll says one million and twenty thousand euros. The manager's ledger agrees, but it follows the seller: one source, not two.",
  "file": "vo/n08_4b80df9cf6.mp3",
  "dur": 9.091,
  "in": 0.043,
  "out": 8.475,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.083,
    2.938
   ],
   [
    3.632,
    5.016
   ],
   [
    5.257,
    6.334
   ],
   [
    6.967,
    7.606
   ],
   [
    7.771,
    8.355
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n09",
  "text": "Bank receipts show nine hundred and fifty-eight thousand. Tenants confirm nine fifty-five.",
  "file": "vo/n09_0580b7fb11.mp3",
  "dur": 5.747,
  "in": 0.028,
  "out": 5.351,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.068,
    2.66
   ],
   [
    3.369,
    5.231
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n10",
  "text": "Cash outranks documents. The quorum settles at nine fifty-six, and the field reaches level A three: reconciled to cash.",
  "file": "vo/n10_3d96ea6cb8.mp3",
  "dur": 8.385,
  "in": 0.012,
  "out": 8.359,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.052,
    1.538
   ],
   [
    1.895,
    3.961
   ],
   [
    4.214,
    6.168
   ],
   [
    6.578,
    7.801
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n11",
  "text": "Counterparties can require a level, field by field, from A zero to A five. And A four needs something new: capital at risk.",
  "file": "vo/n11_27d8019fb1.mp3",
  "dur": 9.273,
  "in": 0.006,
  "out": 8.858,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.046,
    1.815
   ],
   [
    2.016,
    3.046
   ],
   [
    3.327,
    5.058
   ],
   [
    5.618,
    7.312
   ],
   [
    7.674,
    8.738
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n12",
  "text": "A bond is a holdback with rules instead of lawyers. An illustrative deal: thirteen million euros, eight hundred thousand of attested income, a six point one five percent cap rate.",
  "file": "vo/n12_7d188dc040.mp3",
  "dur": 11.311,
  "in": 0.034,
  "out": 10.811,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.074,
    2.823
   ],
   [
    3.287,
    4.413
   ],
   [
    4.578,
    5.983
   ],
   [
    6.271,
    8.326
   ],
   [
    8.598,
    10.691
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n13",
  "text": "The seller warrants that income within five percent, for twelve months. A forty-thousand tolerance.",
  "file": "vo/n13_7d90530875.mp3",
  "dur": 6.165,
  "in": 0.03,
  "out": 5.64,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.07,
    3.523
   ],
   [
    4.114,
    5.52
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n14",
  "text": "The bond covers the buyer's loss at a ten percent miss: eighty thousand over the cap rate. One point three million, held in a yield-bearing escrow.",
  "file": "vo/n14_6cb55dbd21.mp3",
  "dur": 9.43,
  "in": 0.035,
  "out": 8.839,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.075,
    2.914
   ],
   [
    3.497,
    5.176
   ],
   [
    5.528,
    6.702
   ],
   [
    6.878,
    8.719
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n15",
  "text": "Twelve months of bank receipts decide.",
  "file": "vo/n15_1d658ac2dc.mp3",
  "dur": 2.534,
  "in": 0.044,
  "out": 2.207,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.084,
    2.087
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n16",
  "text": "Income of seven sixty is a five percent miss, inside tolerance. The bond is released in full.",
  "file": "vo/n16_6609b8ef58.mp3",
  "dur": 6.635,
  "in": 0,
  "out": 6.272,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.004,
    2.866
   ],
   [
    3.239,
    4.364
   ],
   [
    4.551,
    6.152
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n17",
  "text": "At seven twenty, the miss is five points beyond tolerance. Half the bond goes to the buyer. Pro rata, never all or nothing.",
  "file": "vo/n17_0cd4c65eca.mp3",
  "dur": 8.542,
  "in": 0.018,
  "out": 8.086,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.058,
    3.239
   ],
   [
    3.674,
    5.267
   ],
   [
    5.86,
    6.613
   ],
   [
    6.789,
    7.966
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n18a",
  "text": "That only works where a later truth exists, that a contract can read.",
  "file": "vo/n18a_5605ae1f96.mp3",
  "dur": 4.676,
  "in": 0.064,
  "out": 4.644,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.104,
    2.392
   ],
   [
    2.561,
    3.863
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n18b",
  "text": "Rent against receipts. Title against the registry. Bondable.",
  "file": "vo/n18b_32f64dd5a4.mp3",
  "dur": 4.963,
  "in": 0,
  "out": 4.299,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.0,
    1.234
   ],
   [
    1.524,
    3.173
   ],
   [
    3.654,
    4.179
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n18c",
  "text": "Building condition? Only with a referee, named in advance.",
  "file": "vo/n18c_78e2dea2d4.mp3",
  "dur": 4.598,
  "in": 0.027,
  "out": 4.551,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.067,
    0.954
   ],
   [
    1.605,
    4.009
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n18d",
  "text": "Valuations and opinions: never.",
  "file": "vo/n18d_551112d1c5.mp3",
  "dur": 2.351,
  "in": 0.018,
  "out": 2.322,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.058,
    1.407
   ],
   [
    1.589,
    1.992
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n19",
  "text": "Staking learned this. Slashing works on facts the chain can see, and has failed wherever disputed conduct was put to a vote.",
  "file": "vo/n19_1214d76744.mp3",
  "dur": 8.307,
  "in": 0.004,
  "out": 7.503,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.044,
    1.194
   ],
   [
    1.516,
    3.99
   ],
   [
    4.274,
    7.383
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n20",
  "text": "So who posts the capital? Usually, it isn't new money. The bond replaces the holdback, or W and I premium, a sale already carries.",
  "file": "vo/n20_90c4a4785e.mp3",
  "dur": 10.214,
  "in": 0.009,
  "out": 9.625,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.049,
    1.484
   ],
   [
    2.064,
    3.583
   ],
   [
    4.274,
    5.822
   ],
   [
    6.299,
    7.775
   ],
   [
    8.048,
    9.505
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n21",
  "text": "The seller can self-bond. A surety can post for a fee. Or the buyer can hold a policy, on the same trigger.",
  "file": "vo/n21_2dc87dcbf3.mp3",
  "dur": 7.001,
  "in": 0.021,
  "out": 6.455,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.061,
    1.408
   ],
   [
    1.719,
    3.484
   ],
   [
    3.853,
    6.335
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n22",
  "text": "The market is the middle one: sureties quoting on the same attested record, with fees that fall with level and track record.",
  "file": "vo/n22_d140571cba.mp3",
  "dur": 7.784,
  "in": 0.031,
  "out": 7.211,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.071,
    1.351
   ],
   [
    1.844,
    4.385
   ],
   [
    4.736,
    7.091
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n23",
  "text": "Sellers bond only if certainty, a higher rank, firm debt, speed, is worth more than the cost. That has to be measured, not assumed.",
  "file": "vo/n23_eb4576f152.mp3",
  "dur": 9.326,
  "in": 0.002,
  "out": 8.606,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.042,
    1.912
   ],
   [
    2.174,
    2.926
   ],
   [
    3.12,
    4.37
   ],
   [
    4.691,
    6.053
   ],
   [
    6.619,
    8.486
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n24a",
  "text": "And the native insurer? There are three paths.",
  "file": "vo/n24a_4592d2ec51.mp3",
  "dur": 3.344,
  "in": 0.053,
  "out": 3.199,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.093,
    1.246
   ],
   [
    2.069,
    3.079
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n24b",
  "text": "As for a native insurer: a data partner needs no capital. An M G A underwrites on a carrier's capital. An own carrier needs a licence, and solvency capital. The realistic route is A, then B.",
  "file": "vo/n24b_460ea5bb9e.mp3",
  "dur": 13.505,
  "in": 0,
  "out": 13.282,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.037,
    1.368
   ],
   [
    1.649,
    3.565
   ],
   [
    3.933,
    6.782
   ],
   [
    7.157,
    8.703
   ],
   [
    9.02,
    10.214
   ],
   [
    10.849,
    12.294
   ],
   [
    12.545,
    13.162
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n25",
  "text": "The edge is observation. The platform sees what was claimed at close, and what was realised for years after. That pairing is a loss curve no incumbent has.",
  "file": "vo/n25_bca6ce3724.mp3",
  "dur": 10.109,
  "in": 0.044,
  "out": 9.576,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.084,
    1.369
   ],
   [
    1.813,
    4.003
   ],
   [
    4.27,
    6.192
   ],
   [
    6.747,
    9.456
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n26",
  "text": "So short-tail, parametric cover comes first, because it teaches fastest. Float comes last.",
  "file": "vo/n26_b90df12d51.mp3",
  "dur": 6.635,
  "in": 0,
  "out": 6.38,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.033,
    2.628
   ],
   [
    2.96,
    4.361
   ],
   [
    5.104,
    6.26
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n27a",
  "text": "It's a working draft, and the numbers are illustrative. But the plan is simple.",
  "file": "vo/n27a_55b44d6311.mp3",
  "dur": 4.728,
  "in": 0,
  "out": 4.69,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.0,
    2.455
   ],
   [
    3.049,
    4.147
   ],
   [
    4.606,
    4.69
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "n27b",
  "text": "Measure first. Bond what is measured. Insure the rest.",
  "file": "vo/n27b_435d33b23a.mp3",
  "dur": 4.545,
  "in": 0,
  "out": 4.273,
  "segs": [
   [
    0.016,
    0.828
   ],
   [
    1.443,
    2.527
   ],
   [
    3.147,
    4.154
   ]
  ]
 }
]